    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the August 8 slate with a heavy emphasis on SB-upside, led by the core duo of **Yordan Alvarez** (82.19) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12). **Yordan Alvarez** remains an absolute must-start, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against King, where his xwOBA of 0.473 anchors the heart of our lineup. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is projected for a massive day; despite a slight negative adjustment for facing a pitcher capable of holding runners, his elite sprint speed and prime lead-off spot against the 4.66 xERA of Lugo position him as a high-efficiency engine for our scoring. **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21) also offer strong value, though both carry risk due to a 30% rain probability in their matchup against Scherzer; their high scores are primarily buoyed by the favorable 5.31 xERA of the opposing veteran arm.\n\nTactical platoon advantages are central to today\u2019s strategy, most notably with **Caleb Durbin** (65.55) and **Christian Yelich** (59.82). **Caleb Durbin** earns the UTIL spot over bench alternatives due to a significant park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Jump, while **Christian Yelich** capitalizes on a +13% platoon adjustment, mitigating the sting of a lower order placement. On the bubble, **Jacob Gonzalez** (35.99) and **Chase Meidroth** (34.97) were the closest to cracking the starting nine, but both were relegated to the bench primarily due to sub-40 scores resulting from tough matchups against Stock and Williams, respectively; neither presented a compelling enough case to supersede our high-floor starters. We are closely monitoring **Junior Caminero**, whose status is technically pending, though his assumed #3 spot against Kirby provides enough categorical stability to maintain his place in our active lineup.",
